WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.980
Content that converts: captions, Reels and replies.

2
00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:08.930
This is the video for module two of Social Media Marketing for Business.

3
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:16.630
Every post should have one job. Some help people discover you, some build trust, and some ask for the sale.

4
00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.530
A good photo with no caption telling people what to do next wastes attention.

5
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:28.920
Short vertical video is your best free way to reach new customers, and a phone is enough.

6
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:33.690
And most sales are won or lost in comments and messages.

7
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:49.230
A strong caption has three parts. The hook is the first line, the only part people see before tapping more. Good morning everyone is weak. Your jollof is not watery because of the rice, it is the tomatoes, is strong.

8
00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:57.710
The value is the useful middle: details, benefits, a short story or tips. Write the way you speak to a customer.

9
00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:07.110
The call to action tells people exactly what to do, like send TRAY on WhatsApp to get the price list. Use only one per post.

10
00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:15.510
And give a price range or a from price where you can. Many buyers skip posts that only say DM for price.

11
00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:32.100
Bisi makes adire tote bags in Abeokuta and is launching a new indigo design. On Monday, to be discovered, she posts a 12-second Reel of the bag packed with a laptop. The hook on screen says, fits a 14-inch laptop.

12
00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:42.220
On Wednesday, to build trust, a carousel of 6 slides showing the dye process, the stitching, the pockets, a customer carrying it, and the size.

13
00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:52.200
On Friday, to sell, a portrait photo: from 15,000 naira, approximate, only 10 made, send INDIGO on WhatsApp to order.

14
00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:58.290
She makes all three in one 90-minute session on Sunday and schedules them in Meta Business Suite.

15
00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:12.740
Plan every video in three parts. The hook comes first, because many viewers decide within seconds. Esther in Onitsha opened with tiger nuts poured into a blender, and the words, can it blend tiger nuts?

16
00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:23.870
The body shows the process in short clips, cutting out any waiting. Esther used four 3-second clips, ending with a glass of smooth tiger-nut milk.

17
00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.560
Then the call to action. Available in Onitsha, WhatsApp link in bio.

18
00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:37.550
Film vertically. Wipe the lens, face a window, and rest the phone on books or a tripod so it stays steady.

19
00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:46.630
Add auto-captions, because many people watch with sound off. Music copied from elsewhere can get your video muted or blocked.

20
00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:51.030
Post the clean file on each platform, without another app's watermark.

21
00:02:52.280 --> 00:03:07.110
Stories disappear after 24 hours and reach people who already care about you. Every poll or question reply opens a private chat, a natural moment to sell. Keep prices, reviews and how to order in Highlights.

22
00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:21.910
A Live builds trust fast. Kemi, a fabric seller in Lagos, announced hers with a countdown, held each lace to the light, repeated prices, and pinned her WhatsApp link. Customers ordered the same evening.

23
00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:37.490
Amaka runs a cake business in Enugu. A customer comments that her cake arrived with the top crushed. Within an hour Amaka replies publicly: I am so sorry, I have sent you a message so we can make this right today.

24
00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:42.980
Never delete honest complaints or argue in public. Other customers are watching.

25
00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:51.360
On WhatsApp she asks for a photo and the order details, and learns the rider was stuck in traffic on a hot afternoon.

26
00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:58.880
She offers a free replacement or a 50 percent refund. The customer chooses the replacement.

27
00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:07.450
Then Amaka fixes the cause with insulated boxes. The customer updates her comment to say it was resolved.

28
00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:18.150
During busy Lives, fake payment screenshots and fake bank alerts are common. Release goods only after you see the money in your own bank or payment app.

29
00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:27.840
And protect your customers. Never post a phone number, address or payment detail in comments, and blur personal details in any chat screenshot.

30
00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:43.960
To remember. Give every post one job. Write a hook, value and one call to action. Plan videos as hook, body and call to action. Answer the question first, then move to private chat. And confirm payment before you ship.

31
00:04:45.210 --> 00:04:53.660
Now schedule three posts with three different jobs, make your first Reel, create three Highlights, and save four WhatsApp quick replies.

32
00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:56.160
Then continue with the lessons below.
